# never-stage — paths that must NEVER be committed from this checkout (P-035).
#
# One path or glob per line; `#` starts a comment. Matched against the STAGED
# path list, repo-relative, with forward slashes. Globs: `*` within a segment,
# `**` across segments.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# This repo is ONE folder on ONE branch, and it permanently contains the owner's
# uncommitted local work. `git add <directory>` cannot tell that work from the
# work being committed. On 2026-08-17 a `git add tools/caspar-bridge` swept up
# the owner's plant-testing hack, and `dev` briefly shipped a hardcoded
# `return '192.168.21.93'` in `guessLanHost()` — every install would have
# advertised one machine's LAN address. It was caught in post-push verification
# and cost a second push to correct.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS A NET, NOT A CURE. The cure is the bridge advertise-host refactor,
# which removes the reason the hack exists at all. Until that lands, this file
# stops the same accident recurring.
#
# THE ESCAPE, when a listed file genuinely must be committed:
#
#     CG_ALLOW_NEVER_STAGE=1 git commit ...
#
# It is deliberately loud — the guard prints what it let through, so an
# intentional override is visible in the terminal rather than silent.

# The owner's plant-testing advertise-host hack. See tools/caspar-bridge/src/
# template-http-server.ts `guessLanHost()`. Remove this line when the
# advertise-host refactor lands and the hack is gone.
tools/caspar-bridge/src/template-http-server.ts
